<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry III of Głogów</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1260–<a href="/years/1309">1309</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry III was a Silesian Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> from 1274 and one of the most powerful princes of fragmented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. After the death of Wenceslaus III in 1306 he took most of Greater Poland and styled himself heir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>. At his death in 1309 his lands were divided among his sons, and Konrad I received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olesnica">Oleśnica</a>, which became a separate duchy.</p></div>
